{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/998004-2e-non-affinity-gifts","id":998004,"title":"[2e] Non-Affinity Gifts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-03T18:37:44-07:00","id":998004,"title":"[2e] Non-Affinity Gifts","content":"When I look at the cost of learning a Non-Affinity Gift, I realize 'wow, there's a lot of benefit to joining a Tribe so you can get three more of those things.' I think that because the difference between an Affinity Gift and a Non-Affinity Gift is a full 2xp - the difference between 3 and 5, respectively. But when I make, say, a Rahu and look over the list of things and see the Gift of Rage and all its lovely facets, I think 'I want this so badly.' But I'm not a Blood Talon! I can't take that Gift at the Affinity cost. I worry to myself if I'm losing on other opportunities by not taking it. But I really want it.<br /> <br /> And that's to say nothing of Ghost Wolves, who have only their Auspices to draw on for Affinities...<br /> <br /> For others who have played in Second Edition by now, do you find yourselves having this conflict at times? Have you bitten the bullet and paid the extra cost for that Non-Affinity Gift you were so dearly craving, or did you stick to the Affinity Gifts of your Auspice and Tribe?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T19:13:41-07:00","id":998012,"title":"","content":"I wasn't a fan of my Auspice Gifts at first. My character was technically an Elodoth Iron Master, who ended up breaking into Death Gifts and City Gifts.<br /> <br /> It can seem hard at first, but breaking into a Non-Affinity Gift only has a one-time cost. Once you've gotten the Rage Gift, for instance, outside of the Blood Talons, you get 1 Facet. Then each additional Facet costs 2 Experiences, the same as it does for everyone else.<br /> <br /> The decision was tough for me because my character was very focused on his Primal Urge so once I got that five Experiences it was very tempting to just go Primal Urge with it. But otherwise I don't think it's that hefty a tax, especially since once opened you can get further Facets for free with your Renown.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}